{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Thus you shall say to my lord.</b> He said this to them until it becomes clear to them that he is his master, and they speak with him in the manner of a servant." "<b>and until now.</b> The alef is a sign of the speaker [1st person], and the hidden consonant after it stands in place of the root alef, and likewise \"I love those who love me\" (Proverbs 8:17), for it is heavy on the tongue to produce two alefs, and it is from the light binyan [pa'al]."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:44.623471018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}